  "scope": "Integral Milnor T=0 and the rational four-term Bloch identity are fixed identities, not an irrationality proof. Prime-window/full-gcd no-go results apply only to the specified unbalanced binomial families. Ordinary Rodrigues has proved nonzero and decay exponent but no actual primitive-content theorem. The explicit higher-log candidate has proved moments and uniqueness; endpoint nonzero, actual decay and minimal denominator budget remain open. All-scale claims rely on written proofs; finite certificates, visual identity checks and hashes verify their stated inputs.",
